// Quiz for Lambda
::Lambda::
What are lambda functions in Python?
{
=Functions defined using the lambda keyword for concise, one-line expressions
~Functions that handle exceptions and errors in Python
~Functions used for mathematical calculations only
~Functions that have no return statement
}

::Lambda::
Which of the following statements about lambda functions in Python is true?
{
=Lambda functions can have any number of arguments but only one expression.
~Lambda functions can contain multiple expressions.
~Lambda functions can include a return statement.
~Lambda functions cannot be assigned to variables.
}

::Lambda::
What is the advantage of using lambda functions in Python?
{
~They can handle complex mathematical operations
~They are more memory-efficient than regular functions
=They allow for concise and anonymous function definitions
~They have better error handling capabilities
}

